# Device class and viewport proof

Name the work device before editing: Phone, Computer, or Either. Ledger classifications are proposals; change the class when the real scope requires it.

- Phone work is planning, review, cloud-agent edits, and light preview checks. It does not include local builds, schema changes, secrets, billing actions, or production database access.
- Computer work is local build, terminal, migration, security review, and final verification.
- Either work may start on a phone and finishes on a computer when tests or local simulation are required.

For a user-facing change, state whether acceptance is phone, desktop, or both. A phone preview does not prove desktop. A desktop check does not prove the phone layout. Workout, program, and onboarding changes need both viewports when they change those screens.

Phone work still follows `no-unapproved-main-or-deploy.mdc`.
